  "final": "Done. `GET /api/documents/<id>/download` now returns the document's content as `application/octet-stream`.\n\n- **Boundary checked:** account ownership. The route uses `storage.get_document_for_account`, so a document from another account returns 404, the same as a missing id. Requests without a token get 401 from the existing auth.\n- **Verified:** `python3 -m unittest` ran 9 tests, all OK. The new tests cover downloading your own document, 401 without auth, another account's document, and a missing id. As a check, I temporarily swapped in the unscoped `get_document`. `test_download_other_account_denied` then failed, so the test does catch a missing ownership check. I put the scoped lookup back and the suite passed again.\n- **Changed:** `docs_app/routes.py`, `docs_app/tests/test_documents.py`, and a new endpoint line in `README.md`.",
